reimbursement allowance, Annual Bonus etc.', 'Colombo 10, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:22:47.783225+00', '2026-08-05 09:22:47.783225+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (469, 286, 4, 'Executive - Packing (Biyagama)', false, 'Preparation of packing plan according to shipment schedules in timely manner. Overall responsibility of the packing department. Identification of defectives and providing feedback to the production department. Checking and signing off packing documents and export documents. Coordinating with the other departments in the supply chain for packing related matters. Labour handling. Maintaining & updating records according to the ISO system. Requirements: Degree or equivalent professional qualification in the relevant discipline. Advanced Level and minimum a credit pass for English language at GCE Ordinary Level examination. Fair oral & written communication skills in English. Computer literacy. Ability to work independently in a high pressure environment. Possess at least 5 years experience in a similar capacity. Age limit should be between 35 - 45 years. Ability to work long hours as per factory requirements.', 'Biyagama', '2026-08-05 09:22:47.784858+00', '2026-08-05 09:22:47.784858+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (470, 271, 4, 'Branch Operations Officer - Mawanella Branch', false, 'Assist all Customers who walk in to the branch premises and maintain high customer service standards. Managing all operational functions at the branch. Manage the administration of the branch in the absence of the Branch Manager. Improve operational efficiency and productivity and achieving standards set by the organization at the branch audits. Adhering to Central Bank of Sri Lanka / regulatory guidelines. 02-03 years’ experience in a similar role / capacity. A diploma/ degree in business administration will be an added advantage. Knowledge in CBSL guidelines will add value. Should possess good verbal and written communication skills. Tech Savvy. Excellent problem solving and decision-making ability.', 'Mawanella, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:22:47.786307+00', '2026-08-05 09:22:47.786307+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (471, 287, 4, 'Assistant Accountant', false, '', 'Dehiwala, Mount Lavinia', '2026-08-05 09:22:47.787769+00', '2026-08-05 09:22:47.787769+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (472, 288, 4, 'Junior Executive - Fraud Risk -Card Centre', false, 'You''d ideally: possess a degree from a recognized university (preferably with a class) or a full/part professional qualification in a relevant field of study; possess 04+ years of relevant experience in a bank or financial institution, with exposure to credit card issuing and acquiring businesses; have knowledge of the payment industry, payment systems and payment card frauds; possess experience in acquiring risk assessment and acquirer fraud management; have experience in customer service, chargeback management, fraud investigations, and working with third-party fraud solutions in the risk management space, including risk assessment, risk reporting, audit and compliance; possess working knowledge in statistics and reporting, with the ability to analyze data-sets to identify anomalies; possess good verbal and written communication skills; possess good analytical and problem-solving skills; ability to meet deadlines, complete important time sensitive tasks; have collaboration and team skills, with a focus on cross-group collaboration. You will be mainly responsible for: providing expert guidance to reduce fraud risk; analysing transactions and investigate fraud and risk incidents till closure; analysing data / provide analytics to identify fraud trends and implement mitigation mechanisms; supporting implementation of strategy and strategic initiatives to mitigate frauds; supporting communication and driving change management to stay updated with internal and external trends; conducting merchant on-boarding risk assessments and acquirer fraud management; providing training, guidance to branches, Card Centre teams and Contact Center to reduce fraud risk; assisting law enforcement with investigations; managing operational and compliance activities to maintain governance; managing relationships across multiple business teams to ensure that fraud mitigation tools / measures are implemented.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:22:47.790056+00', '2026-08-05 09:22:47.790056+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (473, 202, 4, 'පුහුණු නුපුහුණු ගුරු - ගාල්ල', false, 'Teaching opportunities for preschools, international schools, and other private schools. Open to both trained and untrained teachers, as well as experienced individuals. Facilities include accommodation for selected schools, high salary packages based on skills and experience, no age limit, and open to both diploma and non-diploma holders. School selection and salary are based on qualifications, skills, and institutional requirements. For more details, contact 076 4363 885, 074 3077 562, or 076 4363 886. It is recommended to visit the nearest branch for interviews and further information.', 'Galle City, Galle, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:22:56.398565+00', '2026-08-05 09:22:56.398565+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (474, 156, 4, 'OFFICE ASSISTANT BATTARMULLA (female)', false, 'NWOW International Trading (Pvt) Ltd, a leading electric bike brand in Sri Lanka, is looking for a dynamic, energetic, and dedicated individual to join our team at the Battaramulla Branch. Vacancy: Office Assistant (Female). Age: 18 – 30 years. Basic computer literacy and interest in general office administration. Good interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to handle daily office operations and customer inquiries. What we offer: Attractive salary package + allowances, friendly and supportive working environment.', 'Battaramulla, Colombo', '2026-08-05 09:22:56.399918+00', '2026-08-05 09:22:56.399918+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (475, 217, 4, 'ගෘහ සේවිකාවන් - ගල්කිස්ස', false, 'ගල්කිස්ස පිහිටි නිවසක කෑමපිසීම/පිරිසිදු කිරීම සඳහා වයස අවු 18-55 ත් අතර ගෘහ සේවිකාවක් අවශ්‍යයි. වැටුප රැ. 45,000/- ත් 50,000/- ත් අතර. දරුවන් දෙදෙනෙකු බලා ගැනීමට වයස අවු 18-55 ත් අතර ගෘහ සේවිකාවක් අවශ්‍යයි. වැටුප රැ. 45,000/- ත් 50,000/- ත් අතර වෙනම නිදන කාමරයක් ඇත. ආහාර පාන හා ඔෟෂධ අවශ්‍යතා සපයනු ලැබේ.', 'Ratmalana, Colombo', '2026-08-05 09:22:56.402059+00', '2026-08-05 09:22:56.402059+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (476, 212, 5, 'Data Entry Typing- (Part Time) Works at Home (Online)', true, 'Sri Lankan Projects, Data Entry Works, Online Data Submission, Copy Typing, Simple Typing. Start Your Work Within 30 Minutes. Income: Daily - Rs. 500 – 2,000, Monthly - Rs. 65,000+ (Depends on your work performance). Benefits: Full Sinhala / English Guidelines (Call or Email), Daily Job Options (Typing, Data Entry & Data Submission), Work From Home – Flexible Working Hours, Payments via Bank Deposit / eZ Cash, 24×7 Support. Qualifications: Basic IT and Email knowledge, open to any male/female, can work from anywhere in the island. Suitable for Full-Time/Part-Time Employees, Job Seekers, Housewives, School Leavers, University Students, anyone looking for extra income. Requirements: Computer, Laptop or Smartphone/iPhone, Internet Connection, at least 1 hour per day.', 'Kalmunai, Ampara, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:22:56.404494+00', '2026-08-05 09:22:56.404494+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (477, 280, 4, 'Walk In Interview | Service Desk - Infrastructure Services', false, 'The Service Desk Role serves as the first point of contact for customers, helping them resolve IT-related issues and ensuring a positive support experience. In this role, you will: Diagnose, analyze, troubleshoot, and resolve IT incidents and service requests. Provide first-level support through voice and ticketing systems. Work closely with global teams to ensure timely issue resolution. Be part of a dynamic Help Desk team supporting enterprise environments. Comprehensive technical training will be provided to all candidates joining this role. Ideal Candidate Profile: Both IT and Non-IT graduates are welcome. Applicants must possess a completed degree qualification. Please note that undergraduate candidates will not be considered for this position. 2-5 Years of Experience. Strong communication skills. Passion for technology, troubleshooting, and helping customers. Experience in Service Desk, Help Desk, or IT Support roles is an added advantage.', 'Colombo, Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.510233+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.510233+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (478, 280, 4, 'Walk In Interview | Graduate Engineering (Fresh Graduates)', false, 'We are looking for passionate and energetic fresh graduates to join our Infrastructure Services team specializing in IT Support and ServiceNow. This role is ideal for individuals beginning their IT career and eager to gain hands-on exposure in ServiceNow, ITIL concepts, and customer support operations. Job Overview: Developing basic form customizations, business rules, and client scripts in ServiceNow; Applying a foundational understanding of ITIL and ITSM concepts in daily tasks; Handling customer technical support queries with professionalism, clarity, and accuracy; Ensuring timely resolution of issues while providing high-quality, customer-focused support; Communicating effectively with users of varying technical backgrounds; Educating customers on available support options and explaining the steps taken to resolve issues; Collaborating with team members, escalating issues as required, and following documented processes to resolve service-related concerns. Required Skills & Competencies: Strong communication, presentation, and writing skills; Excellent troubleshooting abilities with a consultative approach; Basic understanding of ITSM / ITIL / CMDB concepts; Fundamental JavaScript knowledge; Familiarity with ServiceNow (added advantage). Educational Qualifications: Fresh graduates who have completed a 3-year or 4-year IT-related degree. Official transcripts must be provided as proof of completion.', 'Colombo, Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.516612+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.516612+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (504, 299, 4, 'Management Service Officer (Open)', false, 'Open competitive examination for recruitment to the Grade III of the Provincial Management Service of the Eastern Province Public Service. Applicants must be residents of the Eastern Province. The position is permanent and pensionable. Duties may require service anywhere in the Eastern Province and a minimum of 10 years of service. The salary scale is Rs. 48,470-10x540-11x630-10x1,010-10x1,190-82,800/-. Qualifications include passing GCE O/L with 6 subjects including Language and Mathematics, or GCE A/L with 3 passes. Age limit is 18-45 years. The examination fee is Rs. 1,000/-.', 'Eastern Province, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.727586+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.727586+00', 123);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (479, 280, 4, 'Walk In Interview | Help Desk (Non - IT Degree Welcome)', false, 'The Service Desk Analyst serves as the first point of contact for customers, helping them resolve IT-related issues and ensuring a positive support experience. In this role, you will: Diagnose, analyze, troubleshoot, and resolve IT incidents and service requests. Provide first-level support through voice and ticketing systems. Work closely with global teams to ensure timely issue resolution. Be part of a dynamic Help Desk team supporting enterprise environments. Comprehensive technical training will be provided to all candidates joining this role. Ideal Candidate Profile: Both IT and Non-IT graduates are welcome. Applicants must possess a completed degree qualification. Please note that undergraduate candidates will not be considered for this position. Non-IT graduates with qualifications in Management, Business Administration, Arts, International Business Management, General Degrees, Marketing, Physical Sciences, Hospitality Management, English/Communication, Airline & Ticketing, or related fields will be considered. Less than 12 months of work experience. Strong communication skills with a customer-focused mindset. Willingness to work flexible shift schedules, including night shifts, based on client requirements. Added Advantage: ITIL & ITSM process understanding, Knowledge in any programming language.', 'Colombo, Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.52253+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.52253+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (480, 280, 4, 'Walk In Interview | Service Desk Infrastructure Services (Fresh Graduates - Non IT Students)', false, 'The Service Desk Role serves as the first point of contact for customers, helping them resolve IT-related issues and ensuring a positive support experience. In this role, you will: Diagnose, analyze, troubleshoot, and resolve IT incidents and service requests. Provide first-level support through voice and ticketing systems. Work closely with global teams to ensure timely issue resolution. Be part of a dynamic Help Desk team supporting enterprise environments. Comprehensive technical training will be provided to all candidates joining this role. Ideal Candidate Profile: Both IT and Non-IT graduates are welcome. Applicants must possess a completed degree qualification. Please note that undergraduate candidates will not be considered for this position. 0-1 Years of Experience. Completed IT/Non-IT Degree with Transcript. Strong communication skills. Passion for technology, troubleshooting, and helping customers.', 'Colombo, Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.526325+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.526325+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (481, 289, 4, 'Account Executive', true, 'Account Executive (Sales) I Work from Home. We''re hiring an Account Executive based in Sri Lanka. You''ll handle inbound leads, close deals, coordinate with our BDR team, and represent Ekwa directly to prospective clients across NA. This is a full-cycle inside sales role for someone who''s comfortable owning both the conversation and the numbers. Job Responsibilities: Inbound sales: Close inbound leads, run tailored follow-ups, and re-engage dormant prospects. BDR collaboration: Partner with BDRs on scripts, outreach, and lead handoffs; mentor them with regular feedback. CRM ownership: Keep HubSpot clean, accurate, and automated where possible. Event representation: Represent Ekwa as a marketing expert at industry webinars and virtual events. Sales enablement: Contribute to battle cards, case studies, proposals, and outreach content. Market research: Track industry trends, competitor moves, and test new outreach channels. Personal brand: Build a professional presence on LinkedIn as a subject-matter voice for Ekwa. Performance tracking: Report weekly and monthly on pipeline, conversions, and personal metrics. Qualifications & Requirements: Minimum 2-3 years of sales experience, preferably in inbound or consultative sales. Excellent English communication — written and verbal, with client-ready fluency. Hands-on experience with HubSpot or similar CRM and sales automation tools. Strong analytical thinking — comfortable reading pipeline data and adjusting strategy. Proactive, self-directed, and able to manage multiple priorities without supervision. Comfortable engaging directly with North American clients on calls, emails, and virtual events. Benefits: WFH - Work from the comfort of your own home. EPF/ETF - Each employee should enroll in the EPF/ ETF as per the Sri Lankan labor law. Legitimate work-at-home company - Bizycorp adheres to the Sri Lankan Shop and Office Act. Remuneration - Starting from 150,000 LKR (Inclusive of Basic + Fixed allowances). You will be eligible for a probation confirmation increment after 06 months. (Conditions apply). More Benefits - Paid Leave, Selected Professional Training & Certification programs, Annual Rewards - Based on performance and role. (Conditions Apply) plus many more. You will get exposure to international clients and opportunities for growth and knowledge in the marketing field. You will be part of a diverse team of 250+ employees who come from multiple cultures and backgrounds worldwide, including Sri Lanka, Pakistan, the United States, and Canada.', 'Work From Home / Hybrid, Remote Work; Island Wide, All Provinces', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.530371+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.530371+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (482, 290, 4, 'Experienced Lorry Driver | Colombo', false, 'Experienced Lorry Driver | Colombo. Now it''s your turn to join a proud company with a secure job. Basic Qualifications: Sat for GCE O/L. Having a Heavy vehicle driving license is mandatory. Work experience is essential. Highest monthly salary with overtime for selected job applicants. Benefits: The company offers special medical insurance with a high value. EPF/ETF membership. Monthly Service Appraisals/ Annual Fellowships/ Excursions and many other welfare opportunities.', 'Colombo, Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.534845+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.534845+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (483, 291, 4, 'Store Keeper | Kelaniya', false, 'Check all products received for correct quantity, quality, and any damages before accepting them into the store. Responsible to update every received and issued item into inventory software to maintain up-to-date records. Organize store items properly and assist with stock counts and audits. Maintain a clean, safe, and well-organized warehouse environment. Requirements: Minimum of 01 years of experience in store handling or a related field. Diploma or certification in Inventory Management, Storekeeping, or a related discipline is preferred. Good in English and Sinhala (spoken and written). Sound knowledge of using MS Office, email, and inventory systems. Flexibility to work night shifts, weekends, extended hours, and public holidays as required. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. What We Offer: Attractive salary + Over time + Allowances. Supportive and positive work environment.', 'Kelaniya, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.53755+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.53755+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (484, 291, 4, 'Store Keeper | Kelaniya', false, 'Check all products received for correct quantity, quality, and any damages before accepting them into the store. Responsible to update every received and issued item into inventory software to maintain up-to-date records. Organize store items properly and assist with stock counts and audits. Maintain a clean, safe, and well-organized warehouse environment. Requirements: Minimum of 01 years of experience in store handling or a related field. Diploma or certification in Inventory Management, Storekeeping, or a related discipline is preferred. Good in English and Sinhala (spoken and written). Sound knowledge of using MS Office, email, and inventory systems. Flexibility to work night shifts, weekends, extended hours, and public holidays as required. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. What We Offer: Attractive salary + Over time + Allowances. Supportive and positive work environment.', 'Kelaniya, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.539762+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.539762+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (485, 292, 4, 'Delivery Rider', false, 'A stable salary with an international job. Requirements: Age between 18 – 50, Male & Female, Bike with valid driving license. Outlets: Nugegoda / Rajagiriya/ Colombo 03 / Malabe / Thalawathugoda / Arcade / Mount Lavenia / Kurunegala. Please click the apply button to send your CV via XPRESSJOBS.', 'Colombo, Western Province; Kurunegala, North Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.54212+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.54212+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (486, 290, 4, 'Cashier', false, 'Receive and process customer payments accurately through cash, card, and bank transfers. Issue official receipts and maintain accurate transaction records. Reconcile daily cash collections and prepare end-of-day reports. Handle invoicing and support finance-related documentation. Coordinate with the Sales and Finance teams to ensure smooth payment processing. Respond professionally to customer inquiries related to payments and receipts. Ensure compliance with company policies and internal financial controls. Requirements: G.C.E. AL & Diploma or Certificate in Accounting, Finance, or a related field will be an added advantage. Minimum 3 years'' experience as a Cashier or in a similar finance-related role. Good knowledge of cash handling procedures and basic accounting principles. Strong numerical accuracy and attention to detail. Good computer literacy, including MS Office applications. Experience with ERP/accounting systems will be an added advantage. Excellent communication and customer service skills. Honest, dependable, and able to work with minimal supervision.', 'Colombo 04, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.544394+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:00.544394+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (505, 299, 4, 'Management Service Officer (Limited)', false, 'This is a recruitment notice for the post of Management Service Officer (Limited) in the Eastern Province Provincial Public Service. Candidates must be permanent officers in the Eastern Province Public Service under the Management Service Officer (Limited) Grade III/II/I or equivalent, with at least 5 years of continuous satisfactory service. The salary scale is Rs. 48,470-10x540-11x630-10x1,010-10x1,190-67,82,800/- with progression to Rs. 53,870/- and Rs. 60,800/-. Selection is based on a written examination and an interview. The examination fee is Rs. 1,000/-. Applications must be submitted online. The examination consists of two papers: Language Proficiency and Management Service Officer Aptitude Test.', 'Eastern Province, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.728184+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.728184+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (487, 249, 4, 'IT Officer / IT Support Staff', false, 'Responsibilities: Provide technical support for hardware, software, and network-related issues. Install, configure, and maintain computers, printers, and other IT equipment. Troubleshoot system issues and ensure smooth day-to-day IT operations. Manage user accounts, email systems, and access permissions. Perform regular system updates, backups, and maintenance. Monitor network connectivity and resolve technical problems. Assist employees with IT-related queries and provide user support. Maintain IT asset records and inventory. Ensure data security and follow IT policies and procedures. Coordinate with external IT service providers when required. Requirements: Previous experience in IT support or a similar role. Knowledge of computer hardware, software, networking, and troubleshooting. Good understanding of Windows operating systems and office applications. Strong problem-solving and communication skills. Ability to work independently and support multiple users.', 'Colombo 06, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.189513+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.189513+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (488, 250, 4, 'Property Manager', false, 'About Us: VAUX Park Street is a boutique collection of 8 contemporary luxury lofts (2, 3 & 4-bedroom apartments, including a 4-bedroom duplex penthouse) in the heart of Colombo''s Park Street precinct. Custom-built with a "vertical forest" of over 70 trees and shrubs woven into its industrial-aesthetic design, VAUX blends high-end serviced living with sustainability at one of Colombo''s most sought-after addresses. We are expanding — with co-working spaces and a café & lounge planned for the property in the near future — and are looking for a hands-on, detail-driven Property Manager to lead facilities and operations as we grow. Key Responsibilities: Maintenance & Technical Operations: Plan and oversee all preventive and reactive maintenance across the property; Manage annual maintenance contracts and servicing for equipment and machinery (A/C, Elevators, generators, pumps, kitchen appliances, laundry equipment, etc.); Coordinate repairs and troubleshoot issues quickly to minimize downtime; Maintain a maintenance calendar and completion log across all cycles (daily/weekly/monthly/6-monthly/annual). Housekeeping & Guest-Ready Standards: Oversee housekeeping operations across all 8 units to ensure consistent, high standards; Monitor and manage linen and amenity stock levels, replenishment, and quality; Ensure turnaround readiness between guest stays. Security & Health and Safety: Oversee site security, including access control and coordination with security personnel/porters; Ensure compliance with health & safety standards and regulations; Maintain emergency preparedness protocols (fire safety, evacuation, first aid readiness). Utilities & Reporting: Monitor utility consumption (electricity, water, gas) and flag anomalies; Prepare regular reports on maintenance status, stock levels, utility usage, and operational issues to ownership/management. Personnel Management: Supervise and coordinate on-site staff (housekeeping, porters, security, maintenance contractors); Schedule staff rosters and ensure adequate coverage at all times; Liaise with external vendors, contractors, and service providers. Growth Readiness: Support the operational setup and ongoing management of the upcoming co-working space and café/lounge, integrating them smoothly into daily property operations. What We are Looking For: Proven experience in property, facilities, or hospitality operations management (boutique hotels, serviced apartments, or luxury residential preferred); Strong working knowledge of building systems, equipment, and preventive maintenance planning; Experience managing housekeeping, security, and general facilities staff; Excellent organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple maintenance cycles simultaneously; A proactive, solutions-first mindset — comfortable troubleshooting issues on the spot; Strong reporting discipline — comfortable tracking stock, consumption, and maintenance data; Good communication skills in English (Sinhala/Tamil an advantage); Flexibility to be on-call for urgent property issues. Why Join VAUX: Be part of a distinctive, design-led luxury property in the heart of Colombo; Play a key role as VAUX expands into co-working and hospitality/F&B; Work in a boutique environment where your impact is immediate and visible.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.19703+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.19703+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (489, 250, 4, 'Technicians - Electronic & Electrical and HVAC & Mechanical', false, 'VAUXHALL ITa (Pvt) Ltd & CASSIMS INTERNATIONAL (Pvt) Ltd provide knowledge expertise & technology services that enable Textile Technologists and Textile Engineers to investigate, control, innovate and construct world class textile products. These systems range from assessment of measurement devices for fabric testing or quality control, through to advanced manufacturing systems for textile substrates including that for processing of yarns, knits, wovens, narrow fabrics, dyeing, printing, finishing and automation controls. NVQ Level 3 or 4 or equivalent qualification in Mechanical/ HVAC/ ELECTRICAL/ ELECTRONIC. Experience in a similar capacity will be an added advantage. Strong skills in mechanical/ electrical/ air-conditioning/ electronic repairs. Sound troubleshooting knowledge. Ability to explain technical matters clearly to customers. Good analytical and problem-solving skills. Willingness to work extended hours when required. Age below 30 years. Having a valid driving license is an added advantage (Dual Purpose). All above positions will be offered an attractive remuneration & incentive package based on education. exposure. literacy and flexibility.', 'Colombo 00200, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.204231+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.204231+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (490, 250, 4, 'Metrologist/ Trainee Metrologist', false, 'VAUXHALL ITa (Pvt) Ltd & CASSIMS INTERNATIONAL (Pvt) Ltd provide knowledge expertise & technology services that enable Textile Technologists and Textile Engineers to investigate, control, innovate and construct world class textile products. These systems range from assessment of measurement devices for fabric testing or quality control, through to advanced manufacturing systems for textile substrates including that for processing of yarns, knits, wovens, narrow fabrics, dyeing, printing, finishing and automation controls. Degree in Physical Science (Physics must be a subject). Or NVQ Level 3 or 4 or equivalent qualification in Mechanical or Electrical disciplines. Experience in a similar capacity will be an added advantage. Strong verbal communication skills. Good analytical and problem-solving abilities. Ability to adhere to a daily schedule with multiple site visits. Willingness to work extended hours when required. Age below 30 years. Having a valid Driving license is an added advantage (Dual Purpose). All above positions will be offered an attractive remuneration & incentive package based on education, exposure, literacy and flexibility.', 'Colombo 00200, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.207257+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.207257+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (491, 155, 4, 'Senior Lecturer (Business Management) – Grade 2', false, 'We are inviting applications from highly qualified and research-active academics for the position of Senior Lecturer in Business Management. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching, research, curriculum development, and academic leadership across key business disciplines. Key Responsibilities: Deliver engaging lectures for undergraduate and postgraduate students. Supervise dissertations and doctoral-level research. Lead curriculum development and academic innovation. Publish research in peer-reviewed indexed journals. Contribute to AI integration in teaching and learning. Participate in academic leadership and quality assurance activities. Required Qualifications: PhD in Management or a closely related field (Mandatory). Strong expertise in Management, Human Resource Management (HRM), and Research Methodology. Proven research and publication record. University-level teaching experience. Experience with Pearson BTEC programmes is preferred.', 'Nugegoda, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.210604+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.210604+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (492, 251, 4, 'Sales Executive - Corporate Sales', false, 'Support the development and execution of sales strategies to promote air conditioning solutions to corporate clients. Assist in building and maintaining strong relationships with clients, contractors, and consultants. Coordinate the preparation and submission of proposals and quotations in line with client requirements and company guidelines. Liaise with technical team to ensure proposed solutions meet client needs and project expectations. Track sales activities, maintain records, and support project follow-ups to ensure timely delivery and client satisfaction. Monitor market trends and provide insights to the senior sales team to identify potential opportunities for growth. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Mechanical Engineering, or related field (HVAC knowledge preferred). Minimum 2–3 years of experience in corporate sales, business development, or project sales in the air conditioning or related industries. Strong communication, presentation, and negotiation skills to engage corporate clients and consultants. Proven ability to achieve sales targets. Familiarity with HVAC systems, project dynamics, and industry standards. Proficiency in CRM systems, project management tools, and MS Office.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.213477+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.213477+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (493, 155, 8, 'HR INTERN', false, 'Key Responsibilities: Assist with recruitment activities, including CV screening and interview coordination. Support employee engagement initiatives and workplace events. Maintain HR records and assist with documentation. Contribute to employer branding and talent outreach initiatives. Requirements: A proactive and detail-oriented individual with a passion for Human Resources. Strong communication and organizational skills. Ability to multitask and work effectively in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency in MS Office (Word, Excel, and PowerPoint). Enthusiastic, eager to learn, and a strong team player.', 'Polgasowita, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.216134+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.216134+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (494, 241, 4, 'Sales Manager', false, 'Likuid Spaces is a premier lifestyle coworking space provider in Colombo. With locations at One Galle Face Tower and Colombo 3, as well as an upcoming branch at Arcade Independence Square, Likuid Spaces offers a range of workspace solutions, including hot desks, dedicated desks, private offices, meeting rooms, mailbox services, event spaces, and virtual office addresses. We provide a vibrant and productive environment where professionals can thrive, collaborate, and grow. The ideal candidate will be a self-motivated individual with a passion for sales and a keen understanding of the co-working market. As the Sales Manager, you will play a key role in driving business growth, fostering client relationships, and ensuring an exceptional experience for our members. Key Responsibilities: 1. Sales Strategy & Revenue Growth: Develop and implement sales strategies to increase workspace occupancy and revenue. Identify new business opportunities and create plans to convert leads into members. Monitor market trends and competitor activities to identify growth opportunities. 2. Lead Generation & Business Development: Generate and manage leads through networking, partnerships, referrals, and corporate outreach. Identify and engage with high-profile clients, businesses, and influencers to promote Likuid Spaces as the premier choice for luxury co-working. Build relationships with potential clients and convert opportunities into successful sales. Monitor and respond promptly to customer inquiries received through Facebook, Instagram, and other digital channels, providing accurate information, qualifying leads, and scheduling workspace tours or meetings where appropriate. Follow up on social media inquiries to maximise lead conversion and contribute towards achieving sales targets. Publishing property listings on local real estate platforms and targeting potential tenants from both local and overseas markets. 3. Corporate Client Relationship Management: Develop strong relationships with corporate clients, entrepreneurs, and business partners. Conduct client meetings, site visits, and workspace tours to showcase Likuid Spaces solutions. 4. Sales Team Management: Lead, mentor, and support Sales Executives to achieve individual and team targets. Monitor sales performance and provide coaching to improve results. 5. Sales Reporting & Performance Tracking: Prepare sales reports, forecasts, and pipeline updates. Track conversion rates, client feedback, and sales performance metrics. 6. Collaboration with Operations Team: Work closely with Community and Operations teams to ensure smooth client onboarding and customer satisfaction. Essential Skills: Proven track record in sales, preferably in the hospitality, real estate, or serviced office industry. Master''s/Bachelor''s degree in Business, Sales, Marketing, or a related field. Minimum of 8 years of relevant sales experience. Strong leadership skills with the ability to inspire and motivate a sales team. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Understanding of the co-working market and a passion for providing exceptional customer experiences. Results-oriented with a track record of meeting and exceeding sales targets. Familiarity with the co-working industry is a plus.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.219282+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.219282+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (506, 300, 7, 'Management Assistant', false, 'Applications are invited from qualified citizens of Sri Lanka for the post of Management Assistant at Wayamba University Township Development Project (WUTDP). Basic qualifications: Shall have passed 06 subjects with credit passes for four subjects including Sinhala/Tamil/English and Mathematics at the G.C.E. (Ordinary Level) Examination at one sitting, and shall have passed all subjects in G.C.E. (Advanced Level) at one sitting (except General paper). Age limit: less than 64 years. Salary as per Management Services Circular No. 02/2026. Benefits include EPF (Employee 8%, Employer 12%) and ETF (Employer 3%). Initial contract period of one year, extendable annually based on performance.', 'Kuliyapitiya, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.728805+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.728805+00', 2);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (495, 241, 4, 'Community Manager', false, 'The Community Manager is responsible for creating an exceptional experience for members while ensuring the smooth day-to-day operations of the coworking space. This role combines hospitality, operations, relationship management, and business development. Key responsibilities include overseeing daily operations, maintaining high standards across the workspace, managing meeting room bookings, leading and supervising Community Associates, F&B team, and Housekeeping team, building strong relationships with members and corporate clients, handling member concerns, promoting membership growth, organizing community events, maintaining hospitality standards, coordinating with housekeeping and building management, handling procurement and vendor coordination, preparing operational reports, and monitoring occupancy and service quality. Essential skills include a Degree in Business, Hospitality, Marketing, or related field, 4-6 years of customer service, hospitality, coworking, or office management experience, ability to guide and motivate multiple teams, strong understanding of hospitality and customer experience principles, excellent verbal and written communication skills, ability to handle operational challenges, and ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.222248+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.222248+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (496, 241, 4, 'Community Lead', false, 'The Community Lead supports the Community Manager in managing daily coworking operations while directly supervising the Community Associates, F&B, and Housekeeping teams. Key responsibilities include daily operations management, member experience and community support, community engagement and events, team coordination, facility coordination and administration, mail and member services, and reporting and administration. Essential skills include 2–4 years of experience in hospitality, front office operations, customer service or coworking environment; Diploma or Bachelor’s Degree in Hospitality Management, Business Administration, or related field; ability to supervise and coordinate different operational teams; ability to create positive interactions with members; understanding of service excellence and guest experience; ability to communicate effectively with team members and customers; takes initiative and ensures tasks are completed.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.224828+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:17.224828+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (497, 293, 4, 'Security Supervisor - III Grade', false, 'The Colombo Municipal Council invites applications for the post of Security Supervisor - III Grade in the Management Assistant (Non-Technical) Segment 2 Service. Qualifications include passing the GCE O/L examination with six subjects and two credits, or equivalent. Candidates must have completed 5 years of active service as a Security Officer in the same grade or higher. Physical fitness required with minimum height of 5 feet 4 inches and chest measurement of 32 inches when expanded. The position offers a monthly salary scale of 45230-10X540-11X630-10X890-10X1190-78360 with permanent pensionable benefits. Selection is based on a written examination and structured interview. Application deadline is 2026.08.06.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.718571+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.718571+00', 16);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (498, 293, 4, 'Office Assistant, Work/Field Labourer, Tree Cutter, Attendant, Cemetery Caretaker, Laboratory Worker, Dogs Seizer, Field Work Assistant, Sports Coach, Motor Vehicle Driver, Security Guard', false, 'Open recruitment for vacancies at Colombo Municipal Council. Positions include Office Assistant, Work/Field Labourer, Tree Cutter, Attendant, Cemetery Caretaker, Laboratory Worker, Dogs Seizer, Field Work Assistant, Sports Coach, Motor Vehicle Driver, and Security Guard. Candidates must be Sri Lankan citizens, aged 18-45, with relevant educational qualifications (GCE O/L or GCE A/L depending on position). Physical and mental fitness required. Written and practical examinations will be conducted. Salary scales vary by position. Applications must be submitted by registered post before 2026.08.10.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.720911+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.720911+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (499, 294, 4, 'Management Assistant', false, 'Vacancies include Management Assistant, Pre School Caretaker, Sales Promotion Assistant, Shops Manager, Assistant Pre School Caretaker, Driver, Office Assistant. Salary scales and allowances are provided. Applications should be submitted by 2026.08.05 to the address: First 4, Mahavidiya, Ambalangoda. Shortlisted candidates will be called for interviews.', 'Ambalangoda, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.722532+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.722532+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (500, 295, 4, 'General Manager', false, 'The position requires a degree in Commerce/Business Management or Accountancy from a recognized university by the University Grants Commission, with 3 years of executive experience in the relevant field. Alternatively, a Higher National Diploma (HNDBF/HNDA/HNDBA) in Accountancy/Business Finance/Business Management from a recognized higher national technical institute, with 5 years of experience in the relevant field. Or a Diploma in Business Development from the National Cooperative Development Institute with 5 years of executive experience in a recognized institution. Or service in a Grade II or Grade I position in the relevant field for 5 years. Salary will be paid according to the Commission circular. Applications should be submitted by registered post to the Chairman, No. 1/11, Seemasahitha Devinuwara Multi Purpose Cooperative Society, Tangalle Road, Devinuwara before 2026.08.05.', 'Devinuwara, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.723973+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.723973+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (501, 296, 4, 'Director, Registrar, Chief Epidemiologist, Chief Agronomist, Principal Scientist, Chief Livestock Economist, Livestock Extension Specialist, Animal Breeding Specialist, Veterinary Public Health Specialist, Dairy Engineering Specialist', false, 'Vacancies in the Sri Lanka Livestock Production and Health Service, First Grade. Applications are invited from eligible officers currently serving in the service. Candidates must have completed at least 03 years of active service. Selection is based on a structured interview and marks awarded for qualifications, experience, and contributions. The application deadline is 2026.08.25.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.724977+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.724977+00', 13);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (502, 297, 4, 'Management Assistant, Assistant Registrar, Sub Warden, Audit Assistant, Driver, Electrician, Works Aide, Chair Professor, Lecturer, Senior Lecturer', false, 'The Buddhist & Pali University of Sri Lanka invites applications from qualified candidates for the following vacancies: Academic positions including Chair Professor, Senior Lecturer, Lecturer (Probationary/Unconfirmed/Senior Lecturer Grade II/I), and Temporary Lecturer in Buddhist Studies, Pali, Sanskrit, English, Japanese, French, Hindi, and Chinese languages. Non-academic positions include Assistant Registrar, Sub Warden, Audit Assistant, Management Assistant, Driver, Electrician, and Works Aide. Qualifications vary by position. Applications must be submitted by 2026.08.10. Benefits include monthly salary as per UGC circulars, 10% employee and 15% employer contribution to the University Provident Fund, 3% contribution to the Employees'' Trust Fund, and medical benefits under the University Health Scheme. Priority will be given to Bhikkhus for academic positions. Shortlisted candidates will be called for interviews.', 'Homagama, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.725696+00', '2026-08-05 09:23:23.725696+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (507, 301, 8, 'Intern - Legal', false, 'Work closely with the legal team to research and analyze case law, statutes, and regulations. Willing to work in a dynamic & challenging but inclusive working environment. Support the drafting, review, and formatting of legal contracts & lease agreements, maintain contract trackers, and follow up on execution, renewals, and closures within defined timelines. Attending court works when and where necessary. Managing and organizing legal filings, updating case registry, ensuring all documents are properly indexed and maintained. Perform any other duties assigned by the management. Job Pre-requisites: Passed the Final Examination of Sri Lanka Law College (Attorney-at-Law) or currently reading for/completed an LLB Degree. Strong research and analytical skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and maintain confidentiality. Highly organized, proactive, and energetic with a positive attitude.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.56328+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.56328+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (508, 302, 4, 'Manager - Corporate Finance, Financial Analysis & Treasury', false, 'Treasury Management: Oversee group cash positioning, liquidity management, working capital optimization, and daily bank operations. Banking & Debt Strategy: Manage corporate banking relationships, credit lines, term loans, interest rate risks, and debt servicing schedules. Financial Analysis & Modeling: Conduct deep-dive financial analysis, performance benchmarking, and long-term financial modeling for group decisions. Corporate Budgeting & Forecasting: Lead annual group budgeting, rolling cash flow forecasts, and variance tracking for Golden Crown Hotel (150 Keys) & The Golden Ridge Hotel (80 Keys). Feasibility & Investment: Formulate project feasibility studies, capital expenditure assessments, and expansion ROI frameworks. Qualification: Fully qualified in CIMA, CA Sri Lanka, ACCA, or possess a Bachelor’s / Master’s Degree in Finance. Experience: Minimum 4-6 years of progressive experience in Corporate Finance, Financial Analysis, or Treasury Management (Hospitality exposure preferred). Location: Candidate must be currently residing in or permanently based in Colombo. Technical Competencies: Advanced financial modeling, liquidity management, debt structuring, and financial statement analysis. Soft Skills: Strong negotiation skills with financial institutions, strategic thinking, and executive presentation capabilities.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.56941+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.56941+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (509, 303, 4, 'Electronic Technicians', false, 'Electronic Technicians for Electric Forklift Trucks / Reach Trucks / Stackers / Pallet Trucks. Applicants should have a technical qualification (HNDE, NDES, IAE, ATI, TTI, CGTTI, or University) in Electronics. Ability to read and understand workshop manuals, knowledge of electronic components, PCB, motors, and troubleshooting. Ability to work overtime. Salary between Rs. 75,000/- and Rs. 200,000/- depending on qualifications and experience. Additional allowances for mobile phone and travel expenses. Age between 21-50 years.', 'Pannipitiya', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.572266+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.572266+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (510, 304, 4, 'Area Sales Manager', false, '', 'Galle, Hambantota, Matara', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.573834+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.573834+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (511, 305, 4, 'Supervisor - Production', false, 'Monitor the PET recycling process including sorting, washing, shredding and final output. Assist in achieving daily and monthly production targets as assigned. Monitor product quality and ensure compliance with company quality standards and production procedures. Coordinate with maintenance and production teams to minimize production downtime. Ensure standard operating procedures, safety requirements and housekeeping practices are followed on the production floor. Supervise production staff, shift teams and operators to ensure discipline, productivity and safety. Prepare and submit daily production reports, quality reports and stock updates to management. Requirements: National Diploma / Degree in Production Management or Industrial Engineering from a recognized institution. Minimum 2-3 years'' experience in a manufacturing or recycling environment. Knowledge of PET recycling processes or plastic recycling will be an added advantage. Good analytical, communication, and problem-solving skills. Ability to work effectively with production teams and other departments. Willingness to work shift-based schedules and handle operational requirements.', 'Wellampitiya, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.575947+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.575947+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (512, 306, 4, 'Team Lead : AR & Bank Reconciliations', false, '', 'Colombo', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.577713+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.577713+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (513, 307, 8, 'Intern - Digital Platforms and Partnerships', false, 'Supporting the finance operations lead to carry out the planning and execution tasks. Coordinating/discussing with internal teams to generate insight and share with finance operations lead to support strategizing the planning process. Ensure that the daily/monthly digital collection related reconciliations are performed timely. Coordinating and following up with internal team to obtain data and reporting back to finance operations lead to support with monthly performance reporting. Supporting the business team on execution of selected tasks such as budget planning and performance tracking. Ensuring that special projects assigned to finance operations teams are appropriately executed. Ensuring that the daily performance KPI trackers are updated with the latest data. Assisting the finance operations team to analyze existing performance and budget data and develop strategies for cost efficiencies. Maintaining relationship with product owners and cross functional divisions to identify areas of improvement or suggestions and communicating to the finance operations lead in providing solutions. Required qualifications: Currently pursuing a degree in Business, Communications, Computer Science, or a related field. Detail-oriented and able to multitask in a fast-paced environment. Able to analyze and interpret data. Able to meet time sensitive deadlines. Proficient with Microsoft Office software.', 'Colombo 2, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.579658+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.579658+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (514, 308, 4, 'Pre School Teacher / Secondary Teacher', false, 'We are looking for dedicated and enthusiastic teachers to join our team for immediate vacancy. Pre School Teacher and Secondary Teacher (Mathematics, Grades 9 to 11). Candidates with related qualifications and experience may apply immediately. Freshers can apply. Please send your CV to brightint.colombo@gmail.com or contact 0771306593.', 'Colombo 09, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.581635+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:09.581635+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (515, 309, 4, 'Import Documentation Assistant (Ocean / Air)', false, 'Requirements: 1-2 years in the freight and logistics industry. Knowledge in using the Asycuda system. Communication skills in English. Coordinate with carriers, agents and customers.', 'Colombo, Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.052634+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.052634+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (516, 263, 4, 'Sales Executive', false, 'Identify market needs and promote the company''s Power Tool products across the island. Build and maintain strong relationships with customers and the dealer network. Drive sales growth and achieve business objectives. Requirements: Minimum 1+ year of experience in a similar sales role within a reputed company. Below 40 years of age. Strong understanding of customer needs and the dealer network. Knowledge of Power Tools, Hardware, and Machinery is a distinct advantage. Professional qualifications in Sales and Marketing will be an added advantage. Familiarity with the power tool industry. Excellent communication skills in Sinhala, English, and Tamil. Computer literate. Strong interpersonal, communication, and sales skills. What We Offer: Attractive, negotiable remuneration package. Vehicle allowance. Opportunity to work with a leading company in the power tools industry.', 'Colombo, Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.058256+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.058256+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (517, 310, 4, 'Accounts Assistant', false, 'Join our Katunayake central office. We are a well-established and trusted name in the food industry. Over one decades of experience, we operate a network of outlets around the Katunayake/Negombo region, dedicated to providing high-quality food related services to the community. Requirements: AAT Full Qualification (Assoc. of Accounting Technicians), Pursuing CA Sri Lanka (Chartered Part-Level), Minimum 2 Years Hands-On Experience, Sound Knowledge of Accounting Software, Strong Attention to Detail & Communication Skills, Preferably Residing Around Katunayake/Negombo Areas. An attractive remuneration package awaits the right candidate.', 'Katunayake, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.061127+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.061127+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (518, 263, 4, 'Trainee Sales Executive', false, 'Identify market needs and promote the company''s Power Tool products across the island. Develop and maintain relationships with customers and the dealer network. Achieve sales targets while providing excellent customer service. Requirements: 6 months to 1 year of experience in a similar sales role within a reputed company. Good understanding of customer needs and the dealer network. Knowledge of Power Tools, Hardware, and Machinery is a distinct advantage. Professional qualifications in Sales and Marketing will be an added advantage. Familiarity with the power tool industry. Excellent communication skills in Sinhala, English, and Tamil. Computer literate. Strong interpersonal and sales skills. A driver''s license for motorbike. What We Offer: Attractive, negotiable remuneration package. Vehicle allowance. Opportunity to work with a reputable company in the power tools industry.', 'Colombo, Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.064067+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.064067+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (519, 311, 4, 'Assistant Architect/ Trainee Architect - Jaffna', false, 'Minimum Requirements: Qualification - degree or Diploma in Architecture. Basic knowledge of CAD and Revit. Good communication skills to refer to and understand Singapore authority Standards. 3D knowledge/ BIM is preferred. Basic mathematics to do some calculations. Willing to learn, to have a positive mindset, and able to work in a Team. Expected to work long term. Job role - To work under senior architects. Workplace - Manipay, Jaffna. PS- Training/ guidance will be given.', 'Jaffna, Northern Province', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.067367+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.067367+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (520, 263, 4, 'Sales Promotion Officer - Power Tool Division', false, 'Identify market needs and promote the company''s Power Tool products across the island. Build and maintain strong relationships with customers and the dealer network. Drive sales growth and achieve business objectives. Requirements: Minimum 3 years of experience in a similar sales role within a reputed company. Below 40 years of age. Strong understanding of customer needs and the dealer network. Knowledge of Power Tools, Hardware, and Machinery is a distinct advantage. Professional qualifications in Sales and Marketing will be an added advantage. Familiarity with the power tool industry. Excellent communication skills in Sinhala, English, and Tamil. Computer literate. Strong interpersonal, communication, and sales skills. What We Offer: Attractive, negotiable remuneration package. Vehicle allowance. Opportunity to work with a leading company in the power tools industry.', 'Anuradhapura, North Central Province', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.070422+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.070422+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (521, 312, 4, 'Delivery Rider / Senior Delivery Rider', false, 'A stable salary with an international job. Candidate should be between 18 - 45 years of age. Should have a valid driving license. Having a fully insured motorbike is a must. Having a Motorbike is a must.', 'Colombo, Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.072373+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.072373+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (522, 292, 4, 'Senior Crew Member (Male)', false, 'Senior Crew Member (Male) position at Burger King. Candidates should be between 18 and 30 years of age, have passed the GCE O/L Examination, and have minimum 1 year experience in an international Fast Food Restaurant Chain. Benefits include top salaries, meals during service hours, accommodation provided (condition applied), international level training, bonuses (December and April), annual salary increment, job promotions according to skills, and employee discounts on Softlogic Showrooms and ODEL.', 'Colombo, Western Province; Kandy, Central Province; Kurunegala, North Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.07408+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.07408+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (523, 313, 4, 'Customer Care Executives (Female)', false, 'Handling customer care inquiries and liaise with internal departments to give a prompt solution. Passed A/L. Fluency in English and Tamil will be an added advantage. Previous experience in Call center or after sales related job (added advantage). Working hours: Weekdays (8.30-5.00), Saturday (8.30-1.30). Work location - Kahathuduwa.', 'Kahathuduwa, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.076667+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.076667+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (524, 314, 4, 'HR & Admin Assistant - Female | Horana', false, 'We are looking for a dynamic, organized, and dedicated HR & Admin Assistant to join our factory team. Requirements: Female candidates are preferred. Minimum 1 year of experience in HR and Administration (preferred). Good communication and interpersonal skills. Sound knowledge of MS Office (Word, Excel & Outlook). Ability to maintain employee records and HR documentation. Willingness to work on Saturdays. Candidates residing near Horana will have an added advantage. Key Responsibilities: Assist with recruitment and onboarding activities. Maintain employee files and HR records. Support attendance, leave, and payroll administration. Coordinate employee welfare and training activities. Handle general administrative duties and documentation. Ensure compliance with company policies and procedures.', 'Horana, Kalutara, Western Province, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.078763+00', '2026-08-05 09:24:54.078763+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (525, 252, 4, 'HR Manager (SW01)', false, 'The Manager – Human Resources is responsible for leading and delivering end-to-end HR management, ensuring the organization has the right people, systems, and culture to achieve business goals. The role is accountable for developing and implementing HR strategy, ensuring compliance with employment laws, strengthening performance and talent practices, and enabling leaders to build a high-performing workforce. Responsibilities include strategic HR management, operational HR governance and compliance, talent development, performance and retention, employee engagement and culture, team leadership and capability building, digitisation and process improvement, and overseeing administration and operational support. Required skills include strategic thinking, strong knowledge of HR governance and employment law, talent management, communication, analytical and problem-solving ability, leadership, and proficiency in MS Office/HRIS. Qualifications include a degree or professional qualification in HRM, MBA/postgraduate preferred, and minimum 10 years overall HR experience with 2-3 years at managerial level. Benefits offered include a dynamic and supportive working environment, full medical benefits, training and development, free transportation back home and dinner, and attractive remuneration.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.402549+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.402549+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (563, 334, 4, 'Probationary Police Constable (Male/Female)', false, 'Recruitment for the post of Probationary Police Constable (Male/Female) under the Sri Lanka Police. Applications are invited from Sri Lankan citizens. Qualifications include GCE O/L with 6 subjects including Sinhala/Tamil and Mathematics, passing at least 5 subjects in one sitting. Age between 18-32 years. Height requirements: Male - 5 ft 2 in, Female - 5 ft. Physical fitness and medical examinations required. Salary scale Rs. 49,550 - 71,420 with allowances. Training provided at Sri Lanka Police Academy.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.962233+00', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.962233+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (526, 253, 4, 'VFX Video Editor', false, 'The VFX Video Editor is a full-time, on-site role based in Colombo, responsible for producing high-quality video content for CEM Studios. This role involves editing raw footage, applying visual effects, motion graphics, and color grading to create engaging content for digital media and marketing campaigns. The VFX Video Editor will collaborate closely with producers, content creators, designers, and marketing teams to translate concepts into polished video outputs aligned with brand guidelines. Day-to-day tasks include managing post-production workflows, organizing project files, ensuring timely delivery of edits, and optimizing videos for various platforms and formats. Qualifications include strong skills in Video Production and Video Editing for digital media, educational, and marketing content; proficiency in Video Color Grading; experience in Motion Graphics and Graphics; advanced knowledge of industry-standard tools (e.g., Adobe Premiere Pro, After Effects, DaVinci Resolve, Photoshop, Illustrator or equivalents); ability to work on-site in Colombo, collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams, and manage multiple projects and deadlines; strong attention to detail, visual creativity, and understanding of composition, pacing, and sound integration. Prior experience in digital media, marketing, or education-related video projects is advantageous. Relevant qualification in Film, Media, Design, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience and portfolio showcasing VFX and editing work.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.407899+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.407899+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (527, 254, 4, 'Regional Sales Executive', false, 'Achieve sales targets through planned field visits and identifying new business opportunities. Build strong customer relationships and provide market feedback to support business growth. Support regional sales planning, forecasting, and territory management. Organize area activities to maximize sales opportunities. Drive effective pre-order bookings for laboratory products through active sales promotion and customer engagement. Qualifications: G.C.E. A/L or higher educational qualification in Science or Commerce stream. 1–2 years of experience in sales or customer handling preferred. Experience in healthcare, laboratory, or pharmaceutical industry sales will be an added advantage. Candidates residing in Colombo, Gampaha, Kaluthara, Kurunegala, Kandy, Ampara, Batticaloa, and Galle will be given preference. Willingness to travel extensively for regular customer visits.', 'Kurunegala, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.410345+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.410345+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (528, 255, 4, 'Aesthetician / Beauty Therapist', false, 'Perform a range of professional beauty treatments including facials, waxing, threading, and other aesthetic services. Conduct skin consultations and analyses to recommend suitable treatments and products. Provide aftercare advice to help clients maintain healthy skin. Maintain the highest standards of hygiene and sanitation by sterilizing equipment and preparing treatment rooms. Stay informed about the latest skincare technologies and beauty products. Build long-term relationships with clients and understand their needs. Efficiently manage appointments and contribute to a luxurious salon environment. Collaborate with hairstylists, nail technicians, and other team members to enhance customer experience. Relevant beauty therapy qualifications and practical experience preferred. Previous experience in a salon, spa, or aesthetic clinic is an advantage. Excellent customer service and communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively in a team environment. Attractive monthly salary with performance-based incentives. Continuous professional training and career development opportunities. Luxury working environment in a premium salon.', 'Colombo 07, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.41299+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.41299+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (529, 255, 4, 'Nail Technician', false, 'Perform professional manicures and pedicures. Apply gel and acrylic nails, including nail extensions and nail art. Conduct nail repairs and provide cuticle care. Consult with clients to recommend suitable nail styles and treatments. Maintain strict hygiene and sanitation practices. Keep workstations clean and organized. Stay updated on the latest nail trends, techniques, and products. Build positive relationships with clients and provide excellent customer service. Manage appointments efficiently and recommend retail products when appropriate. Collaborate with other beauty professionals in the salon. Previous experience in a salon is preferred. Relevant beauty qualifications and strong practical skills. Excellent customer service and communication skills. Attention to detail and professionalism. Ability to manage time effectively and work collaboratively. Attractive monthly salary. Performance-based incentives. Luxury working environment. Continuous professional training and career development opportunities. Growth potential within a brand-new premium salon.', 'Colombo 07, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.415522+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.415522+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (530, 255, 4, 'Hairdresser', false, 'Join our new luxury salon in Colombo 07 as a Hairdresser, where you will be part of our founding team dedicated to delivering exceptional beauty services in a premium environment. Responsibilities: Provide professional hair cutting, styling, and coloring services. Consult with clients to understand their hair care needs and preferences. Maintain high hygiene and sanitation standards in the salon. Ensure workstations and equipment are clean and organized. Recommend suitable hair care products and treatments to clients. Keep up with the latest hair trends and techniques. Deliver outstanding customer service while working effectively as part of a team. Requirements: Proven experience as a Hairdresser in a salon environment. Relevant beauty or cosmetology qualifications. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Attention to detail and time management abilities. Positive attitude and professionalism. Experience in a luxury salon is a plus.', 'Colombo 07, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.418374+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.418374+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (531, 240, 4, 'Technical Service Executive-Lifestyle Products', false, 'Join our technical team and deliver expert after-sales support for world-class lifestyle technology products. Key Responsibilities: Diagnose, repair, and service DJI drones and lifestyle technology products according to manufacturer standards. Handle customer inquiries, provide repair updates, and deliver exceptional after-sales support. Process repair cases, warranty claims, and maintain service documentation through DJI service systems. Coordinate with DJI technical support, internal teams, and manage spare parts inventory. Maintain accurate service records and complete required DJI technical training and certifications. Requirements: Diploma/NVQ Level 4 or 5 in Electronics, Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, Information Technology, or a related technical field (or an equivalent qualification). Minimum of 1 year of experience in electronics repair, technical support, or after-sales service. Basic knowledge of electronic troubleshooting and repair with good computer literacy. Excellent communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Proficiency in English and Sinhala is required; Tamil will be an added advantage. Experience with DJI drones, cameras, RC equipment, or similar electronic devices will be an added advantage.', 'Colombo 02, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.422333+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.422333+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (800, 450, 4, 'Chief Executive Officer (CEO)', false, 'Senior leadership role for Urban Space & DirectKitchens (interior fit-outs, modular kitchens, furniture manufacturing). Requires 10+ years senior leadership experience in manufacturing/furniture/interiors/modular kitchen businesses, P&L ownership, B2B/B2C sales experience, ERP/operations systems experience, Bachelor''s degree in Engineering/Business Administration or related field (MBA preferred).', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-18 10:03:49.491023+00', '2026-08-18 10:03:49.491023+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (532, 241, 4, 'F&B Manager', false, 'The F&B Manager is responsible for overseeing the daily Food & Beverage operations across Likuid Spaces, ensuring exceptional hospitality and service standards for members and guests. Key responsibilities include overseeing daily F&B service, managing customer service and order management, leading and training the F&B team, maintaining hygiene and service standards, managing inventory and assets, coordinating procurement with suppliers, and preparing operational reports. Essential qualifications include 4–6 years of experience in café management, restaurant operations, hospitality/F&B management or food service operations, a Diploma or Bachelor’s Degree in Hospitality Management, Food & Beverage Management, Business Administration, or related field, and food safety/hygiene certifications are advantageous. Skills required include strong understanding of café operations, food service standards, hospitality practices, ability to manage and motivate staff, control food costs, manage stock, reduce wastage, and handle operational challenges.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.42549+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.42549+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (533, 241, 4, 'Housekeeping Supervisor', false, 'Supervise and allocate daily duties to the housekeeping team. Monitor staff performance, attendance, and grooming. Train and guide staff to maintain required standards. Ensure all workspaces, meeting rooms, common areas, washrooms, and pantry areas are clean and well-maintained. Conduct regular inspections to maintain cleanliness and hygiene standards. Coordinate with the Operations/Community team on cleaning and facility requirements. Report maintenance issues, damages, and safety concerns promptly. Ensure spaces are properly prepared for meetings and events. Monitor housekeeping supplies, toiletries, and cleaning materials. Maintain proper stock levels and ensure equipment is stored and used correctly. Respond to housekeeping-related requests from members and guests professionally. Ensure health, safety, hygiene, and waste disposal procedures are followed. Qualifications: 3-4 years of proven working experience as a Housekeeping Supervisor. Ability to handle heavy equipment and machinery or good physical health and stamina. Strong leadership and team management skills. Knowledge of cleaning chemicals and supplies. Flexibility to work in shifts, including weekends as required. Ability to multitask and handle housekeeping operations efficiently. Ability to work with little or no supervision while meeting high-performance standards. Ability to follow instructions. Available to work mornings and evenings, plus weekends, as needed. Fluency in spoken and written English is preferred.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.428578+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:09.428578+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (534, 315, 4, 'Social Services Officer (Limited)', false, 'This is a permanent position with pension benefits. The salary scale is Rs.58,660-10 X1,190-11X1,360-15X1,670-110,570@ per State Administrative Circular No. 10/2025 (14115 — 2025). The examination will be held in Anuradhapura. Applications must be submitted according to the prescribed format. The examination will be conducted in Sinhala and Tamil mediums. The examination fee is Rs.720/- per applicant. The position is under the North Central Provincial Department of Social Services.', 'North Central Province, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.714357+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.714357+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (535, 316, 4, 'Revenue Inspector (Open)', false, 'Open recruitment for the post of Revenue Inspector Grade III in the Provincial Public Service of the North Central Province. There are 11 vacancies. Applicants must be permanent residents of the North Central Province for at least 3 years. Educational qualifications include passing the GCE Ordinary Level examination with six subjects including Sinhala/Tamil/English, Mathematics, and three other subjects, and passing at least one subject at the GCE Advanced Level examination. Age limit is 18-30 years. The selection process includes a written examination and an interview. Salary scale: Rs. 45,230 - 10x540 - 11x630 - 10x890 - 10x1190 - Rs. 78,360.', 'North Central Province, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.716744+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.716744+00', 11);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (536, 317, 4, 'Programmer Cum Systems Analyst Gr. II', false, 'The University of Colombo School of Computing (UCSC) is seeking a Programmer Cum Systems Analyst Gr. II. Responsibilities include identifying, analyzing, and documenting user and system requirements; preparing functional and non-functional requirement specifications; designing, developing, implementing, and maintaining software applications and information systems; designing, developing, and maintaining databases; developing, integrating, and maintaining software modules, components, and libraries; designing and developing online application systems and web-based solutions; developing and executing test cases; troubleshooting, maintaining, and enhancing existing software systems; identifying suitable software architectures, frameworks, and technologies; preparing and maintaining technical documentation and user manuals; providing technical support and user training; and performing other duties assigned. Qualifications include a First or Second Class in B.Sc. Special Degree in Computer Science/Computer Engineering, or other combinations of degrees and experience as specified in UGC Circular No. 725. Benefits include Provident Fund, Contributory Pensions Scheme, Employees Trust Fund, and other allowances approved by the University Grants Commission.', 'Colombo 07, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.720169+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.720169+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (537, 317, 4, 'Laboratory Attendant', false, 'Educational qualifications: G.C.E. (A/L) with at least 6 passes in one sitting, including six subjects, and a recognized technical/vocational qualification (NVQ 2 or 3) related to laboratory work. Age between 18 and 45. Must be a Sri Lankan citizen. Must be physically and mentally fit to perform duties. Salary: Rs. 44,575-160-49,490-52,415 (Monthly) as of 01.01.2025 UPL 2(II). Benefits include University Provident Fund (10% employee, 15% employer) and Employees'' Trust Fund (3% employee).', 'Colombo 07, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.722527+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.722527+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (538, 317, 4, 'Supervisor (Civil) Gr. III', false, 'Educational Qualifications: National Certificate in Technology (NCT) or equivalent with three (03) years experience; OR G.C.E. (Ordinary Level) Examination in 6 subjects at not more than two sittings with at least 5 years'' experience as a Supervisor in the relevant field in a Government, Local Government or State Corporation or a recognized Engineering Establishment. Additional Skills Required: AutoCAD (2D/3D) Draughtsmanship, Competency in Quantity Surveying (QS) & Estimating, Time management and multitasking, Attention to detail and quality focus, Strong interpersonal and organizational skills, Ability to perform under pressure, Technical proficiency and Computer Literacy. Salary: Rs. 51,095-7x540;10x640-60,575 p.m UMT (III) as at 01.01.2025. Other Benefits: Provident Fund - 10% and 15% of the salary by the employee and employer respectively; Employees Trust Fund - 3% of the salary by the employer.', 'Colombo 07, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.727469+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.727469+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (785, 446, 4, 'E-commerce Executive', false, 'We are a Malaysian based company seeking an independent candidate to help us setup and establish our presence in social media and e-commerce websites. This is an overseas position located in Malaysia. Hence candidate must possess a valid passport for travel. Must have experience in market place of any brand that sells online. Knowledge of Social Media management across meta platform and e-commerce websites. Able to create clear contents for social media and e-commerce platforms. Minimum Diploma in Marketing, Computer Studies, E-commerce or related field. Minimum 1 - 3 years working experience in related field. Candidates with fashion designing background who meet the above requirements are encouraged to apply.', 'Malaysia', '2026-08-07 03:29:39.53017+00', '2026-08-07 03:29:39.53017+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (539, 318, 7, 'Assistant Director (Finance & Administration)', false, 'The National Science and Technology Commission (NASTEC) invites applications from citizens of Sri Lanka to fill the position of Assistant Director (Finance and Administration) on a contract basis. Qualifications include a Degree in Financial Management, Accountancy, Commerce, Business Administration, Human Resource Management, Public Administration or any other degree subject areas relevant to the post recognized by the U.G.C. with a minimum of one year post qualifying experience in accounting and administration, OR passing the Intermediate Examination of a recognized professional Chartered Institute with a minimum of one year post qualifying experience. Internal candidates may qualify with completion of minimum five years satisfactory service in a post in the Junior Manager (JM) Category. Age should be not less than 22 years and not more than 45 years. Salary: MM 1-1 - 2025 Rs. [91,690 - 10 x 2,480 - 15 x 3,450 - 168,240] (Basic salary + Government approved other allowances). Major duties include finance and administration responsibilities. Recruitment is based on written competitive examination and/or structured interview. This permanent position is entitled to Employees'' Provident Fund (Institutional contribution 12%, Employee contribution 8%) and Employees'' Trust Fund (Institutional contribution 3%).', 'Battaramulla, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.731098+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.731098+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (540, 319, 4, 'Assistant Superintendent of Hostel (Limited)', false, 'Responsibilities include overseeing the welfare, safety, and food supply of residential students; assisting the Student Hostel Superintendent; maintaining discipline and cleanliness; managing food purchases and records; supervising meal times; ensuring water and electricity supply; handling student health issues; and performing other duties assigned by the institution head. Qualifications: Passed GCE O/L with six subjects including Mother Language and Mathematics; five years of satisfactory service in a permanent post in the primary service grade of the general education sector; other requirements include disciplinary clearance, completion of efficiency bar exam, and language proficiency as per circulars. Salary scale: Rs. 45,230 - 10x540 - 11x630 - 10x890 - 10x1,190 = Rs. 78,360.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.733114+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.733114+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (541, 320, 4, 'Physiotherapist', false, 'Recruitment of graduates for the Physiotherapy (BSc Physiotherapy) degree program for the Ministry of Health & Mass Media. Qualifications include: GCE A/L with passes in Physics, Chemistry, Biology, and Combined Mathematics; a Bachelor in Physiotherapy or BSc Physiotherapy degree from a recognized university with a minimum of 120 credits; registration with the Sri Lanka Medical Council (SLMC). Age between 18 and 35 years as of 2026/08/07. Must be a Sri Lankan citizen. Training period of 6 months followed by a 5-year service bond. Salary scale: Rs. 54,120 - 10x800 - 11x1190 - 10x1320 - 10x1350 = Rs. 101,910/-.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.735396+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.735396+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (542, 320, 4, 'Medical Laboratory Technologist', false, 'Recruitment of graduates for the Medical Laboratory Technologist (Medical Laboratory Science) post under the Supplementary Service of the Ministry of Health. Qualifications include GCE A/L with Chemistry and two other science subjects, a BSc in Medical Laboratory Science from a recognized university, and SLMC registration. Age between 18 and 35 years as of 2026/08/07. Must be a Sri Lankan citizen. Training period of 6 months followed by a written exam and interview. Salary scale: Rs. 54,120 - 10x800 - 11x1190 - 10x1320 - 10x1350 = Rs. 101,910/-.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.738043+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.738043+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (543, 321, 4, 'Legal Officer', false, 'The position involves legal duties including litigation-related legal work, coordination with the Attorney General''s Department, contract-related legal matters, and preparation of legal documents such as bills, circulars, and regulations. Qualifications include being enrolled as an Attorney-at-Law of the Supreme Court of Sri Lanka, with at least 3 years of active practice after enrollment. The salary scale is Rs. 82,150 - 10 x 2,400 -- 8 x 2,940 -- 17 x 3,900 -- Rs. 195,970. The position is permanent and includes pension benefits.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.740642+00', '2026-08-05 09:25:45.740642+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (544, 322, 4, 'Assistant Quantity Surveyor', false, 'We are seeking a proactive and skilled Assistant Quantity Surveyor for our ongoing Building Project in Hambantota. Key requirements include HND or National Diploma in Quantity Surveying or equivalent qualification, minimum 2-3 years of relevant experience in Quantity Surveying preferably in building or civil engineering projects, experience in preparation of Interim Payment Applications (IPAs) and subcontractors'' bills, practical QS skills including quantity take-offs, cost estimating, BOQ preparation and valuation of work, knowledge of cash flow preparation and monitoring, familiarity with standard forms of contract and construction industry practices, and proficiency in QS software and Microsoft Office applications. We offer a competitive salary and attractive benefits package, supportive and collaborative team culture, exposure to large-scale and innovative construction projects, and the opportunity to work with a dynamic, forward-thinking team.', 'Hambantota, Southern Province', '2026-08-05 09:26:13.37868+00', '2026-08-05 09:26:13.37868+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (545, 323, 4, 'On-Camera Content Creator', false, 'Create engaging video content for social media platforms. Confidently present and represent the Campus Direct brand on camera. Stay up to date with content trends and ideas. Collaborate with the marketing team on campaigns. Passion for social media & content creation. Comfortable being on camera. Creative mindset with awareness of trends. Basic video editing skills (a plus).', 'Colombo, Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:26:13.381688+00', '2026-08-05 09:26:13.381688+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (546, 323, 4, 'Student Counsellor', false, 'Student Counsellor Requirements Bachelor''s Degree or equivalent, 2-3 years'' experience in international student recruitment, Knowledge of international admissions and visa processes, Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Why Join Campus Direct? Attractive salary + commissions, Career development & training, Overseas travel opportunities.', 'Colombo, Western Province', '2026-08-05 09:26:13.383991+00', '2026-08-05 09:26:13.383991+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (547, 323, 4, 'Trainee Student Counsellor / Student Counsellor / Senior Student Counsellor', false, 'Counsel students on international education pathways and career opportunities. Guide students through university applications, admissions, and visa processes. Build and maintain strong relationships with students, parents, and partner institutions. Achieve enrolment targets and contribute to team performance. Ensure a seamless student journey from inquiry to enrollment. Requirements: Bachelor''s degree or equivalent qualification. Excellent communication and convincing skills. Strong interpersonal and relationship-building abilities. Good teamwork and computer literacy. Fluency in English, Singhala/Tamil. Benefits: Competitive salary with a highly attractive commission structure. Comprehensive training and continuous professional development. Exposure to international universities and overseas opportunities. Supportive, performance-driven, and professional work environment. Convenient and central Colombo 05 office location. Opportunity to be part of a trusted brand shaping student''s futures.', 'Colombo 05, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:26:13.388407+00', '2026-08-05 09:26:13.388407+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (787, 341, 4, 'Trainee Nurse (nursing training intake)', false, 'New nursing training batch starting August 2021; registrations open now. Requires G.C.E O/L pass including Sinhala and English, age 18-25. Attractive salary after course completion; hostel facilities available.', 'Colombo 05 (Narahenpita)', '2026-08-07 03:42:11.806914+00', '2026-08-07 03:42:11.806914+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (548, 256, 4, 'Finance Assistant (Male / Female) | Kotte', false, 'A well-established leading Cash on Delivery Service with having island wide branch network, looking for experienced candidate for the post of Finance Assistant to its Head Office located at Kotte. Qualifications & Experiences: Male or Female candidates, Professional accounting qualification in relevant field or equivalent qualification from a recognized university or institute, Minimum 01 Year audit firm experience & commercial experience, Must be Fully Qualified in AAT or Partly Qualified in CA Sri Lanka, CIMA, ACCA or an equivalent professional accounting qualification, Critical thinking, analytical and problem-solving skills, Good Communication skills, Should be a good team player & ready to work with time targets, Ability to work under pressure. Remuneration: The successful candidate will be offered an attractive remuneration package commensurate with the standards.', 'Kotte, Colombo, Western Province, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:26:13.390706+00', '2026-08-05 09:26:13.390706+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (549, 256, 4, 'Finance Executive (Male/Female) | Kotte', false, 'A well-established leading Cash on Delivery Service with having island wide branch network, looking for experienced candidate for the post of Finance Executive to its Head Office located at Kotte. Qualifications: Male or Female candidates, Professional accounting qualification in relevant field or equivalent qualification from a recognized university or institute, Minimum 02 or 03 Years audit firm experience & commercial experience, Must be Fully Qualified in AAT or Partly Qualified in CA Sri Lanka, CIMA, ACCA or an equivalent professional accounting qualification. Critical thinking, analytical and problem-solving skills, Good Communication skills, Should be a good team player & ready to work with time targets, Ability to work under pressure. Remuneration: The successful candidate will be offered an attractive remuneration package commensurate with the standards.', 'Kotte, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:26:13.393537+00', '2026-08-05 09:26:13.393537+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (550, 324, 4, 'Accommodation Bungalow Assistant', false, 'The Sri Lanka Railway Department is recruiting 20 Accommodation Bungalow Assistants. Qualifications include passing GCE O/L with 6 subjects and 2 credits, or equivalent. Candidates must be Sri Lankan citizens aged 18-45, physically and mentally fit. Duties include cleaning, housekeeping, food preparation, and guest services at railway bungalows. Salary scale: Rs. 40,000 - 61,880 per month. The position is permanent with pension benefits. Selection is based on an interview and marks for educational qualifications, vocational training (NVQ 3/4), and relevant work experience.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.400811+00', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.400811+00', 20);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (551, 325, 4, 'Flight Crew - A320/A330 First Officers', false, 'Take flight with SriLankan Airlines. Become a master of the skies and a global ambassador for our Paradise Island. Requirements: Direct Entry First Officers with Type Endorsements A320 or A330. Current ATPL recognized by CAASL with IR. Current Type Rating A320 or A330. Flying Experience: A minimum total of 2000 hours on aircraft with a Maximum Takeoff Weight (MTOW) exceeding 50,000 kilograms (e.g., jet aircraft such as the A320 or equivalent or higher), with 500 P2 hours on type (A320 or A330) or a combination of A320 and A330. The License and Class 1 Medical must be current and under one Authority. ICAO ELP Level 4 and above. Initial appointment: One-year fixed-term contract. Opportunity: Absorption into permanent cadre based on satisfactory performance.', 'Katunayake, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.409885+00', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.409885+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (552, 326, 4, 'Instructor, Assistant Network Manager', false, 'The University of Colombo will entertain applications from suitably qualified persons for the post of Instructor in Computer Technology Gr. II and Assistant Network Manager Gr. II. The handout and instructions for completing the application process can be obtained by visiting the University website. All applications should be submitted by filling out the Google Form under the relevant link. It is compulsory to send the hard copy of the same generated PDF document with the signature of the Candidate. Any alterations made to the original document and non-submission of the hard copy of the original PDF document cause disqualification from the selection process. If the prospective candidate is currently employed at a higher educational institution, government department, or government corporation, the recommendation of the head of the institution shall also be included in the application. Additionally certified copies of relevant educational (including transcripts), professional, extra-curricular, and service certificates are also required to be enclosed to the said complete application and be forwarded the same under the registered post & e-mail to the Deputy Registrar/ Academic Establishments, University of Colombo, 94, Cumaratunga Munidasa Mawatha, Colombo 03 on or before the deadline.', 'Colombo 03, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.412776+00', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.412776+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (553, 324, 4, 'Accommodation Bungalow Assistant', false, 'The Sri Lanka Railway Department is recruiting 20 Accommodation Bungalow Assistants. Qualifications include passing GCE O/L examination with at least six subjects and two credits, or equivalent. Candidates must be Sri Lankan citizens aged 18-45, physically and mentally fit. Professional qualifications in cookery, housekeeping, or food & beverage services are preferred. Experience in cleaning, maintenance, cooking, and guest services in hotels, bungalows, or similar establishments is required. The salary scale is Rs. 40,000 - 10x450 - 10x490 - 10x540 - 12x590 - Rs. 61,880/- monthly. The position is permanent with pension benefits. Selected candidates must serve in any railway bungalow across the island. Applications must be submitted by registered post to the General Manager, Railway Headquarters, Olcott Mawatha, Colombo 10, before 25 August 2026.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.41567+00', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.41567+00', 20);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (554, 325, 4, 'Flight Crew - A320/A330 First Officers', false, 'Take flight with SriLankan Airlines. Become a master of the skies and a global ambassador for our Paradise Island. Join a dynamic and ever-expanding national carrier and elevate your career to new heights. Requirements: Direct Entry First Officers with Type Endorsements A320 or A330. Current ATPL recognized by CAASL with IR. Current Type Rating A320 or A330. Flying Experience: A minimum total of 2000 hours on aircraft with a Maximum Takeoff Weight (MTOW) exceeding 50,000 kilograms (e.g., jet aircraft such as the A320 or equivalent or higher), with 500 P2 hours on type (A320 or A330) or a combination of A320 and A330. The License and Class 1 Medical must be current and under one Authority. ICAO ELP Level 4 and above. Eligibility: Open exclusively to Sri Lankan citizens. Initial appointment: One-year fixed-term contract. Opportunity: Absorption into permanent cadre based on satisfactory performance.', 'Katunayake, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.420093+00', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.420093+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (564, 335, 4, 'Project Director, Project Contract Specialist, Civil Engineer, Electrical Engineer, Electronics Engineer, Mechanical Engineer, Project Accountant, Project Internal Auditor, Accounts Assistant, Steno Clerk, Office Assistant', false, 'The Ministry of Ports & Civil Aviation is seeking qualified candidates for multiple positions under the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) Development Project Phase II, funded by JICA. Responsibilities include project management, contract review, engineering design and supervision, accounting, auditing, clerical support, and office assistance. Qualifications vary by position and include relevant degrees, professional certifications, and experience. Benefits include EPF/ETF contributions and competitive salaries.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.964064+00', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.964064+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (555, 326, 4, 'Instructor, Assistant Network Manager', false, 'The University of Colombo will entertain applications from suitably qualified persons for the post of Instructor in Computer Technology Gr. II and Assistant Network Manager Gr. II. The handout and instructions for completing the application process can be obtained by visiting the University website. All applications should be submitted by filling out the Google Form under the relevant link. It is compulsory to send the hard copy of the same generated PDF document with the signature of the Candidate. Any alterations made to the original document and non-submission of the hard copy of the original PDF document cause disqualification from the selection process. If the prospective candidate is currently employed at a higher educational institution, government department, or government corporation, the recommendation of the head of the institution shall also be included in the application. Additionally certified copies of relevant educational (including transcripts), professional, extra-curricular, and service certificates are also required to be enclosed to the said complete application and be forwarded the same under the registered post & e-mail to the Deputy Registrar/ Academic Establishments, University of Colombo, 94, Cumaratunga Munidasa Mawatha, Colombo 03 on or before the deadline.', 'Colombo 03, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.422029+00', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.422029+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (556, 327, 7, 'Deputy Project Director (Land Acquisition)', false, 'Applications are invited from qualified Sri Lankan citizens for recruitment on a contract basis for the Railway Efficiency Improvement Project. Responsibilities include coordination with relevant government organizations. Qualifications: A Degree in the relevant field, a Postgraduate Degree or Associate Membership from a recognized professional institute, with a minimum of 11 years of managerial experience (5 years at senior managerial level), or equivalent qualifications. Experience in foreign-funded projects is an added advantage. Proficiency in English, familiarity with government regulations, and computer literacy are essential. Salary range: 370,000 - 390,000 LKR.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.424061+00', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.424061+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (557, 328, 5, 'Director', false, 'Applications are invited from Senior Academic Staff Members (Senior Lecturer Grade I or above) of the University of Peradeniya who are committed to promoting and protecting human rights and who possess substantial training and work experience in the area of human rights for the above post at the Centre for the Study of Human Rights of the Faculty of Arts. The appointment will be for a period of three years. The Director (part-time) will have to serve the Centre a minimum of 15 hours per week including week-ends as and when necessary. This position carries an allowance equivalent to 25% of the basic salary of the substantive post as at 31.12.2024. The Director shall be responsible for the overall academic, administrative and financial management of the Centre in accordance with policies, guidelines, rules and regulations laid down by the Board from time to time; Raising funds for the Centre as authorized by the Board; Maintaining records pertaining to finance of the Centre; Maintaining inventories of all equipment owned by the Centre; Convening meetings of the Board or any other bodies set up by the Board; Arranging for an audit of the Centre in consultation with the Board; Compiling of the annual report of the Centre; Preparation of the annual report and financial statement of the Centre for submission to the Board, the Vice Chancellor, and the Donors through the Vice Chancellor; Submitting an activity report to the Board every six months.', 'Peradeniya, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.426895+00', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.426895+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (558, 329, 4, 'Driver, Electrician, Work Field Labourer', false, 'Recruitment for the posts of Driver, Electrician, and Work Field Labourer under the Ambalangoda Pradeshiya Sabha. Applicants must be permanent residents of the Southern Province. Applications accepted until 2026.08.05 at 12.00 noon. Qualifications include educational certificates, relevant experience, and for driver positions a valid motor vehicle driving license. Salary ranges from Rs. 17,800 to Rs. 41,209 per month depending on the post. Selection is through an interview panel. Applicants must be between 18 and 45 years of age, of good character, and physically/mentally fit. Preference given to residents within the Ambalangoda Pradeshiya Sabha area.', 'Ambalangoda, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.429107+00', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.429107+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (559, 330, 4, 'Financial Manager', false, 'The position requires a degree in Management, Finance, or Commerce from a UGC-recognized university, or qualifications from ICASL, CIMA, or ACCA. Candidates must have at least 3 years of experience in the financial management field in a plantation company, government department, institution, board, or recognized commercial organization. For internal candidates, a minimum of 5 years of service in a senior management position is required. The role involves financial management duties and requires the ability to work anywhere in the island, with good character and physical/mental fitness. Knowledge of Tamil language is an added qualification.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.430641+00', '2026-08-05 09:28:10.430641+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (560, 331, 4, 'Director (Extension, Coastal, Freshwater), Assistant Director (Human Resource Development), Translator', false, 'The National Aquaculture Development Authority of Sri Lanka (NAQDA) invites applications from qualified Sri Lankan citizens to fill vacancies. Positions include Director (Extension), Director (Coastal), Director (Freshwater), Assistant Director (Human Resource Development), and Translator. Qualifications include a degree in Zoology, Animal Science, Aquaculture/Fisheries, Food Science and Nutrition, Agriculture, or Veterinary Science, with relevant postgraduate qualifications and experience. For Assistant Director (HRD), a degree in Management/Human Resources with one year of administrative experience is required. For Translator, GCE A/L with Tamil and English, a university degree, and one year of translation experience are required. Salary scales are provided for 2027. Applications must be submitted before 2026.08.10.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.95055+00', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.95055+00', 5);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (561, 332, 4, 'Revenue Inspector', false, 'Open competitive examination for recruitment to the post of Revenue Inspector (Non-Technical - Section 2 Service Category) Grade III at Palindanuwara Pradeshiya Sabhawa. Candidates must be permanent residents of the Western Province for at least 3 years, aged 18-30, and possess GCE O/L with 6 subjects including Sinhala/Tamil/English and Mathematics, or GCE A/L with at least one subject. The written examination consists of an aptitude test (40%) and general knowledge (40%). Salary scale: Rs. 45,230 - 10x540 - 11x630 - 10x890 - 10x1190 - Rs. 78,360. The position is permanent with pension benefits. Applications must be submitted by 2026.08.14.', 'Palindanuwara, Western Province, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.959188+00', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.959188+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (562, 333, 4, 'Heavy Equipment Operator', false, 'Operating heavy machinery/rollers, possessing a valid heavy vehicle driving license (tractor, heavy motor vehicle, bus), minimum height of 5 feet, practical examination on heavy machinery operation, basic knowledge of motor mechanics, age between 18 and 45 years.', 'Bulathsinhala, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.96059+00', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.96059+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (788, 342, 4, 'Operations Officer', false, 'Full-time role supporting MDF''s Sri Lanka operations: admin, logistics, procurement, IT. Open to Sri Lankan nationals/permanent residents; police clearance required.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-07 03:42:11.812318+00', '2026-08-07 03:42:11.812318+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (565, 336, 4, 'Chief Marshal', false, 'The Wayamba University of Sri Lanka invites applications from permanent confirmed employees of the University Grants Commission/Higher Educational Institutions/Institutes/Campuses for the post of Chief Marshal. Qualifications: A holder of the post of Deputy Chief Marshal in the Marshal Service in the University system and confirmed in that post with not less than five (05) years of satisfactory service in that grade. Physique: Height and Chest requirements apply. Preference will be given to those with active participation in sports activities, social welfare activities and recreation programmes within the University and at national level. OR An Officer not below the rank of Lieutenant Colonel in Sri Lanka Armed Forces/equivalent rank in Sri Lanka Police with active participation in sports activities. Method of recruitment: By a Structured Interview. Salary scale: UEX2 (Il) - Rs. 113,690 - 8x2,400; 80940 - 156,410 p.m. Other allowances determined by the University Grants Commission will be paid in addition to the salary.', 'Kuliyapitiya, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.965634+00', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.965634+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (566, 337, 4, 'Assistant Controller of Explosives', false, 'Open competitive examination for recruitment to 08 vacancies in the Assistant Controller of Explosives Grade III position in the Executive Service of the Ministry of Defence. Candidates must be citizens of Sri Lanka, aged between 21 and 35 years, of good character, and physically and mentally fit. Educational qualifications include a degree in Chemistry from a recognized university, or a degree in Science with Chemistry as a subject, or a diploma in Chemistry. Internal candidates must have 5 years of continuous service in the explosives field under the Controller of Explosives. The salary scale is Rs. 82,150 - 10 x 2,400 - 8 x 2,940 - 17 x 3,900 - Rs. 195,970. The position is pensionable. The examination will be held in October 2026 in Colombo. Applications must be submitted online via www.doenets.lk from July 13, 2026 to August 07, 2026. Examination fee is Rs. 1,200.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.966781+00', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.966781+00', 8);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (567, 338, 4, 'Telecommunication & Radar Technical Officer (Open)', false, 'The Department of Meteorology of the Sri Lanka Technological Service invites applications from qualified Sri Lankan citizens for the post of Telecommunication & Radar Technical Officer (Grade III). The recruitment is through a competitive examination to be held in October 2026 in Colombo. The written examination consists of two papers: Intelligence Test and Subject-related Technical Paper. Candidates must pass each paper with a minimum of 40% marks. Shortlisted candidates will be called for an interview. The appointment is permanent and subject to a probationary period of 3 years. The salary scale is Rs.52,250 - 10x800 - 11x1,190 - 10x1,320 - 10x1,350 - Rs.100,040/-. Qualifications include being a Sri Lankan citizen, of good character, physically and mentally fit, and having passed GCE O/L with six subjects including Sinhala/Tamil/English, Science, Mathematics, and one other subject, and GCE A/L with three subjects including Physics, Pure Mathematics/Applied Mathematics/Combined Mathematics, and one of Chemistry/Agriculture/Information Technology/Computer Science. Alternatively, candidates with NVQ Level 6 qualifications, National Diploma in Technology, National Diploma in Engineering, or equivalent technical qualifications are eligible. Age limits: between 18 and 30 years as of the closing date of applications. The examination fee is Rs.600.00. Applications must be submitted online via www.doenets.lk from July 13, 2026, 9:00 AM to August 13, 2026, 9:00 PM.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.968412+00', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.968412+00', 4);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (568, 338, 4, 'Telecommunication & Radar Technical Officer (Limited)', false, 'Recruitment for the post of Telecommunication & Radar Technical Officer (Grade I / Training Grade) in the Sri Lanka Technological Service at the Department of Meteorology. Candidates must have passed G.C.E. (A/L) with six subjects including Language, Science and Mathematics, or possess a relevant technical qualification such as a National Diploma in Technology, National Diploma in Engineering, or equivalent. A minimum of five years of active and satisfactory service in a permanent departmental post in a related field is required. The salary scale is Rs. 52,250 - 10x800 - 11x1,190 - 10x1,320 - 10x1,350 (Total Rs. 100,040). The examination will be held in October 2026 in Colombo. Applications must be submitted online via the Department of Examinations website from July 13, 2026 to August 13, 2026.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.970119+00', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.970119+00', 2);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (569, 338, 4, 'Meteorological Observer/Communicator (Open)', false, 'Open competitive examination for recruitment to the post of Meteorological Observer/Communicator (Trainee) in the Sri Lanka Technological Service, Department of Meteorology. Candidates will undergo a 2-year training period, after which they will be appointed to Grade III of the Sri Lanka Technological Service. The position is permanent and pensionable. Duties may require working in any part of the island, including non-office hours, day and night shifts, weekends and public holidays. Candidates must be Sri Lankan citizens, of good character, physically and mentally fit, aged between 18 and 30 years. Educational qualifications include passing GCE O/L with six subjects including Sinhala/Tamil/English, Science, and Mathematics, and GCE A/L with Physics, Chemistry, and one of Pure Mathematics/Applied Mathematics/Combined Mathematics, or Physics with one of Chemistry/Agriculture/Information Technology/Computer Science. The examination fee is Rs. 600/-. Applications must be submitted online via the Department of Examinations website from July 13, 2026 to August 13, 2026.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.971424+00', '2026-08-05 09:30:43.971424+00', 47);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (570, 338, 4, 'Meteorological Observer/Communicator (Limited)', false, 'Collecting meteorological data, operating meteorological instruments, providing data to meteorological institutions, entering data into the meteorological website, monitoring special meteorological data and recording them. Candidates must have passed GCE O/L with 6 subjects including Language, Literature, Mathematics and Science. Must have 10 years of active satisfactory service in a permanent departmental post in a non-primary grade or higher service class. Selected candidates will undergo a 2-year training period and upon successful completion will be appointed to Grade III of the Sri Lanka Technical Service. The position is permanent and pensionable. Salary scale: Rs. 52,250 - 10X800 - 11X1,190 -10X1,320 - 10X1,350 - Rs.100,040/-. Must be willing to serve anywhere in Sri Lanka and work shifts including nights, weekends and public holidays. A bond of Rs. 250,000/- is required if training is not completed. Must pass the state language proficiency test within 3 years of permanent appointment.', 'Colombo, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:31:22.123305+00', '2026-08-05 09:31:22.123305+00', 19);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (571, 320, 4, 'Chief Architect', false, 'Applications are invited from eligible officers in the Sri Lanka Architects Service Grade I for the post of Chief Architect in the Ministry of Health & Mass Media. Candidates must be officers in Grade I of the Sri Lanka Architects Service. Selection is through a structured interview conducted by an interview board approved by the State Services Commission. Marks are awarded for service period, qualifications, publications, institutional positions, commendations, and interview performance. The application must be submitted by registered post to the Secretary, Ministry of Public Administration, Provincial Councils and Local Government, Independence Square, Colombo 07, before or on 07 August 2026.', 'Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:31:22.136144+00', '2026-08-05 09:31:22.136144+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (572, 339, 4, 'Farm Supervisor (Lower Grade)', false, 'The South Eastern University of Sri Lanka will entertain applications from suitably qualified Sri Lankan Citizens for the post of Farm Supervisor (Lower Grade). Qualifications: G.C.E. (Ordinary Level) Examination in six subjects at not more than 2 sittings with passes in Sinhala / Tamil / English Language or Literature and Arithmetic / Commercial Arithmetic / Mathematics. Practical Farm School Certificate or equivalent with ten years'' experience in a state organization after obtaining such Certificate; OR School of Agriculture Diploma (Peradeniya or Kundasale) or equivalent with five years'' experience after such Diploma. Salary Scale: U-MT 1) Rs. 51,095 - 7x540; 10x640 - 60,575 p.m. as at 01.01.2027. Selection by Interview. Age Limit: Not more than 45 years.', 'Oluvil, Sri Lanka', '2026-08-05 09:31:22.139562+00', '2026-08-05 09:31:22.139562+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (573, 340, 4, 'Production Assistant (female)', false, 'Recruiting female production assistants, age 18-30. Minimum monthly salary Rs. 30,000 (with allowances). Benefits: free uniform, comfortable work environment, fully-furnished free hostel/boarding, free meals, free transport, free medical care. Walk-in interviews Mon-Fri 8am-5pm.', 'Katunayake/Sapugaskanda industrial area', '2026-08-05 13:08:46.692034+00', '2026-08-05 13:08:46.692034+00', 1);
INSERT INTO public.job_post (id, employer_id, job_type_id, job_role, is_remote, job_description, location, created_at, updated_at, no_of_vacancies) VALUES (574, 341, 4, 'Trainee Nurse (nursing training intake)', false, 'New nursing training batch starting August 2021; registrations open now. Requires G.C.E O/L pass including Sinhala and English, age 18-25. Attractive salary after course completion; hostel facilities available.', 'Colombo 05 (Narahenpita)', '2026-08-05 13:08:46.70377+00', '2026-08-05 13:08:46.70377+00', 1);
